      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Metal phenolic networks (MPNs) were used for the first time for the construction of core@shell MOF materials. Diverse functional nanocores with different shapes and sizes could be coated with ZIF-8 shells mediated by MPNs. The obtained Fe3O4@TA-Fe3+@ZIF-8 powder showed a superhydrophobic nature which could efficiently absorb n-hexane from water."},
